  "data_abstract": "CERN-LHC. Measurements of correlations between event-by-event fluctuations of amplitudes of anisotropic flow harmonics in nucleus-nucleus collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{_{\\rm NN}}}=2.76$ TeV, obtained for the first time using a new analysis method based on multiparticle cumulants in mixed harmonics, so-called Symmetric Cumulants (SC). Data was recorded in November 2010 with the ALICE detector at the CERN Large Hadron Collider. The measurements are performed in the central pseudorapidity region (|$\\eta$| < 0.8) and transverse momentum range 0.2 < $p_T$ < 5.0 GeV/c.\n",
